ts with Vatly","\u002Fintegrations\u002Fbolt","4.integrations\u002F2.bolt",{"id":288,"title":34,"body":289,"description":486,"extension":487,"links":488,"meta":489,"navigation":490,"path":35,"seo":491,"stem":36,"__hash__":492},"docs\u002F1.guides\u002F4.authentication.md",{"type":290,"value":291,"toc":482},"minimark",[292,297,319,322,345,349,352,395,398,402,405,473,478],[293,294,296],"h2",{"id":295},"api-keys","API keys",[298,299,300,301,305,306,313,314,318],"p",{},"To authenticate with the Vatly API, you need to include your API key in the ",[302,303,304],"code",{},"Authorization"," header of each request. You can obtain your API key from the ",[307,308,312],"a",{"href":309,"rel":310},"https:\u002F\u002Fmy.vatly.com",[311],"nofollow","Vatly dashboard"," under ",[315,316,317],"strong",{},"Developers » API keys",".",[298,320,321],{},"Vatly provides separate API keys for live and test environments:",[323,324,325,336],"ul",{},[326,327,328,331,332,335],"li",{},[315,329,330],{},"Live keys"," are prefixed with ",[302,333,334],{},"live_"," and are used for production requests.",[326,337,338,331,341,344],{},[315,339,340],{},"Test keys",[302,342,343],{},"test_"," and are used for testing and development.",[346,347,348],"note",{},"Use your test API key during development to avoid affecting live data. Switch to your live API key when you're ready to go to production.",[298,350,351],{},"Here's how to authenticate your requests using cURL:",[353,354,360],"pre",{"className":355,"code":356,"filename":357,"language":358,"meta":359,"style":359},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","curl https:\u002F\u002Fapi.vatly.com\u002Fv1\u002Fcheckouts \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer live_your_api_key_here\"\n","Example request with API key","bash","",[302,361,362,379],{"__ignoreMap":359},[363,364,367,371,375],"span",{"class":365,"line":366},"line",1,[363,368,370],{"class":369},"sBMFI","curl",[363,372,374],{"class":373},"sfazB"," htt